WEBVTT

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.570
Huki leaves are a spring 
food that can be eaten raw.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.800
Ainu children enjoy them as 
snacks when they're out playing.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.980
But the area around your lips 
turns black when you eat them,

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.040
so people can tell you did.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.540
To the Ainu, there are only really 
two seasons: winter and summer.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.790
Winter is the men's season, when they
go into the mountains to hunt.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.770
And when the ice melts and turns to water,

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.420
the women's season, matnepa, comes.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.300
That's when you pick lots of 
herbs and vegetables to preserve.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.760
You prepare during summer, 
so you won't have to worry

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.840
about starving in the long winter to come.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.390
From now on, the women in every 
kotan are about to be very busy.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.740
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:00.030
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:06.810
<b>Yuubari</b>

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.280
<i>Oh, looks like somebody's here.</i>

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.780
You can stay seated.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.050
Who could be here this early?

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.480
Hello.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.060
Do you need something?

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.390
Good morning.

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:28.730
I've heard you deal in taxidermy.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.770
Yes, that's right.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:34.070
Please, come inside.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.940
I have a lot I can show you.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:42.620
<b>Edogai Taxidermist</b>

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.690
Thank you.

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:48.750
I was hoping to get some mounts 
for the 7th Division's guesthouse.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.260
You're as good as the rumors say.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:54.020
<b>Episode Thirteen
Edogai-kun</b>

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.450
There are so many good pieces,
I don't know what to choose!

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.770
Even a polar bear.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:00.720
Sometimes I just import the pelts and 
put them over models I make here.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.330
Is this one still being worked on?

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.230
Why is it upside down?

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:11.230
If you hang them like that, the skin and 
feathers plump up and make it more realistic.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:15.200
The true test of a taxidermist's 
skill is how well

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.650
he can recreate what they 
looked like in life.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:19.460
If you don't mind my asking,

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:23.890
is there sufficient demand for taxidermists 
in Yuubari to sustain your business?

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.540
A kitty!

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.660
It's a kitty!

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:31.740
No, most of my business comes from overseas.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.930
Wealthy people all over the 
world want taxidermy mounts

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:36.210
of animals you can only find in Japan.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.350
I was born in Nara originally,

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:42.380
but I moved to Hokkaido, where the 
temperature is low and the air is dry,

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:46.100
in an attempt to improve my craft.

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.990
You live alone here in Yuubari?

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.810
No, I live with my mother.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.070
I'm afraid she has a bad hip,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.020
and stays in the back.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.480
Oh no, don't worry about it.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.080
I see.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.780
The most important part of a good 
mount is having fresh materials.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:09.250
In other words, you need fresh corpses.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.130
You're very particular about your work 
and take a great deal of pride in it.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.890
The ideal craftsman!

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:18.590
No, I...

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:22.470
Edogai-kun...

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.800
I came to give you your glove back.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:33.650
<i>Oh, what could that sound be?</i>

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:35.940
<i>Something seems strange.</i>

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:38.440
<i>Yasaku-san, did you hurt yourself?</i>

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.400
<i>Are you all right?</i>

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.280
It's nothing!

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.470
I just dropped a mount!

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.560
I've never seen that glove before.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.370
It's not mine.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:54.050
You thought you'd escaped 
us last night, correct?

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:57.450
We pretended we'd lost you, 
and then followed you here.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.670
Edogai-kun...

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:06.510
Think he's got it?

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:10.040
There was a rumor several months ago about 
a coal miner who'd died in an accident,

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.020
a man with a strange tattoo.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:17.020
We dug up the grave, but it was empty.

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:22.210
Which means it was stolen by a grave robber.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.650
Drifters often end up working as miners, 
and they often don't survive long.

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:30.950
The air here is cool and dry,
and bodies don't rot even when buried.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:34.820
Which means that Yuubari is an 
excellent source of fresh corpses.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:38.380
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.280
Leave!

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.480
Night after night you dug up 
fresh corpses from the graveyard,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:49.330
stripping off their skin to 
make this glove, didn't you?

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.780
Wonderful!

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.730
Can I have one, too?

00:04:59.010 --> 00:04:59.940
What?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:04.150
Even after heavy use, it's still 
comfortable and soft against the skin!

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.250
And it fits perfectly, 
right down to the tips of the fingers,

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:08.360
so your fingers can move freely 
enough to pick up tiny coins!

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.910
I've never seen a leather
glove like this before!

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:14.870
You didn't come to arrest me?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:18.380
Catching grave robbers isn't my job.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.730
I'm sorry.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:27.300
That glove isn't made from human skin.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.510
It's pigskin.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.200
Pigs?

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:34.020
The "nails" were made from 
pig hooves and glued on.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.900
To tell you the truth, 
I'd gone to the graveyard

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:42.020
to dispose of a large amount 
of waste products from my work.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.890
I thought you'd found me.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:46.850
All right.

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:50.120
If you like it that much, you can have it!

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.870
I have more. I'll go get one.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:59.880
<i>You seem to be having a good time out there.</i>

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.250
Yes, I am.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.880
<i>But you just met him, right?</i>

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.530
<i>It's not a good idea to trust him easily.</i>

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.240
<i>That's not true.</i>

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.230
<i>Yasaku-san's a great judge of character!</i>

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:12.390
<i>No, it's better to be careful!</i>

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.570
<i>That's why you have no friends.
 You talk like that.</i>

00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.140
Quiet, everyone.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:22.150
Hello, everyone.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:31.820
Are these all made from 
pigskin, too, Edogai-kun?

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:33.500
<i>Kill him.</i>

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.520
<i>He's seen us.</i>

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:35.160
<i>Kill him.</i>

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.160
<i>Stuff and mount him.</i>

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.090
<i>Kill him.</i>

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.880
<i>Kill him!</i>

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.700
<i>Kill him!</i>

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.260
<i>Kill him!</i>

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:50.840
They look like they could 
come to life at any moment!

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.260
You're a genius, Edogai-kun!

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.550
<i>Don't trust him, Yasaku-san!</i>

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.230
<i>He's a bad man!</i>

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:00.390
But, Mom, he's...

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.620
Are you the only one who can hear her voice?

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:05.750
<i>Kill him!</i>

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.480
<i>Now that he's seen us, he cannot leave alive!</i>

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.990
That's what you always say! You try 
to drive everyone away from me!

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.910
You killed Dad, and he was my friend!

00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:20.040
It's not healthy to spend all 
day talking to stuffed corpses.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.930
<i>Shut up, plate-for-brains!</i>

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.900
<i>Your father was a bad man,
 just like all the other men!</i>

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:26.790
<i>Nobody loves you!</i>

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.710
Shut up!

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.550
<i>That's why I castrated you, because you 
looked like your father down there!</i>

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.720
Edogai-kun, listen to my voice.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.310
<i>It was all for you!</i>

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.200
Stop it, please!

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.730
<i>I did it all for you!</i>

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.400
Edogai-kun!

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:48.530
Incredible...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.410
That's human skin, isn't it?

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.240
Yup. What do you think?

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.710
I made it by ripping skin 
off from bodies myself.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.000
<i>Don't open your heart to him!</i>

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.850
Shut up, Mom!

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.790
Shall we talk in your workshop?

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.840
You may not have done the "sen" 
process correctly during tanning.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.220
"Sen"?

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:20.390
The process of scraping off pieces of fat 
and meat that are still stuck to the skin.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:23.390
If you're not careful when you 
do it, the work won't last.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.890
Your skin's a little rough here.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:28.410
Did you use alum when you tanned it?

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:29.370
Yes.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:32.110
That's not good for people 
with sensitive skin.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:35.240
I recommend tannic acid!

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.600
It's plant-based, so it's easy on the skin.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:40.970
Edogai-kun, if you have 
any more of your work,

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.540
would you try it on for me?

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.670
Really?

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:52.230
What do you think, Tsurumi-san?

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.680
I love it!

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.970
It's wonderful, Edogai-kun!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.430
I love it!

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:04.180
That's cutting-edge fashion, Edogai-kun!

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:05.780
I want to see more!

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:08.860
I want to see more of 
your wonderful clothing!

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:13.150
A kitty! Walk like a kitty!

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.320
It's so cute!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.340
What the hell is going on?

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.330
Huh?

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.010
No dice.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.840
It's gotta be Lt. Tsurumi's.

00:09:36.390 --> 00:09:39.200
Oops... Youhei's ear.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.510
Huh? Wait, what?

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.330
So much fun!

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.160
Mom!

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.000
<i>No!</i>

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:47.890
There's the ear!

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:49.910
What are you doing to Mom?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.770
Here, take it.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:56.820
Shoot your mother.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.990
<i>What sort of terrible son 
points a gun at his mother?!</i>

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.700
Decide! Of your own free will!

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:04.500
No...

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.910
<i>No! Don't shoot!</i>

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.610
You have to leave your nest.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:09.120
Your nest was a twisted place,

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:10.980
and that's why you grew up twisted!

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.460
<i>Don't do it!</i>

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.830
The voice... stopped.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:25.810
My mother died of a heart attack.

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:29.140
I should've ended things while she was alive.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:32.560
Thank you.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:37.010
By the way, I wanted to 
make a deal with you.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:38.490
What is it?

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:44.560
The tattooed skins that you and I are
 wearing right now are part of a code.

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:49.000
I want to make false skins, 
bearing nonsense.

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:54.630
I want you to make several clever 
fakes that only we can identify.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:11:01.390
We're going to bring real chaos 
into this war for the tattoos.

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:05.060
<b>Otaru</b>

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:09.730
We've got tattoos from me, 
Ushiyama Tatsuuma, Ienaga here,

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:14.650
Hijikata Toshizou, and two 
copies made on oiled paper.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:19.150
And the one Ogata Hyakunosuke 
acquired in Barato.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.220
That's six in all.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:24.600
So the goal's to get a 
bunch of weirdos, old men,

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:27.470
and thugs together to 
restore the Ezo Republic?

00:11:27.470 --> 00:11:29.650
If this is some petty dream of revenge,

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:32.840
that's not fair to the people 
who are following you.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:38.670
Nopperabo is an Ainu, right?

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:44.090
Did Lt. Tsurumi know that?

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.640
There was one thing in 
common about the belongings

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:51.060
of all seven of the men Nopperabo killed.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.600
They were damaged.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:58.080
Ainu funerals involve destroying or damaging 
the items the dead are buried with,

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:04.590
ending their role in this world so 
that they can be used in the next.

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:11.200
He ripped the bodies apart, but took 
time to damage everything they owned.

00:12:11.200 --> 00:12:14.080
It feels, in a way, like atonement.

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:18.000
The seven who were murdered were sent
 from villages from all over Hokkaido.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:22.110
They were going to use the gold to 
buy weapons to fight the Japanese.

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:26.680
If Nopperabo was trying to help the 
Ainu gain independence for Hokkaido,

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.850
why did he kill them?

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:33.270
Did he betray them because he 
wanted the gold for himself?

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:38.150
My guess is that Nopperabo is a partisan
 from the far eastern part of Russia,

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.940
who was pretending to be Ainu.

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:44.660
Russia is far from a unified place.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.170
There's the forces of the czar,
Lenin's Communist Party,

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:52.450
and then there's the partisans, composed of
 some of the ethnic minorities.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:57.170
Each one of these groups 
is fighting the others.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:03.720
So Nopperabo was a partisan, trying to 
gain funds for a war of independence.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.180
He tried to move the money 
out via Sakhalin, but failed.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:10.140
And that's how this whole thing got started?

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:15.560
You never trusted Nopperabo 
at all, did you, old man?

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:20.530
Which means that No-Face's 
allies outside the prison...

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:26.410
...are very likely to be partisans 
pretending to be Ainu, too.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.990
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:36.040
The masu salmon have come back 
to the rivers again this year.

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:39.470
Sugimoto, you were eating huki, weren't you?

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.090
So were you!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.050
So were you, Asirpa-chan.

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:45.640
You're kidding me.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:46.720
How?

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.190
Asirpa-chan, you ate too much!

00:13:52.710 --> 00:13:54.280
This is masu salmon ohau,

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:56.690
the most delicious food 
you can eat in spring.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.570
Let's eat!

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.480
Hinna, hinna.

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.710
It's great!

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.860
The pukusa is so sweet!

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:09.560
We survived the long winter 
by eating dried foods,

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:14.200
so it's wonderful when spring comes 
and you can eat fresh foods again.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.380
The huki's a little bitter,

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:18.710
but it's sweet and delicious.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.490
It's the taste of spring, sweet and bitter!

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.890
Tell me about Mommy.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.230
Again?

00:14:44.930 --> 00:14:48.450
She was a beautiful woman, just like you.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:50.630
We met in Otaru.

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:53.910
She taught me all the things I didn't know.

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:56.330
The words of the Ainu who lived here,

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.660
and everything they believed.

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.500
My blood, and the blood of 
the Ainu who live here...

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:07.460
You're a mix of both, so you'll 
be a new kind of Ainu woman.

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:12.340
And you'll be the leader of the Ainu.

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:15.650
Your eyes are the same as mine.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.980
Never forget what I'm about to tell you.

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:26.980
Shiraishi, wake up!

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:29.070
How long are you going to 
keep sleeping, you pig?

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:31.490
We're leaving.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.300
Yuubari's still a long way off.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:36.080
You seem upset this morning.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.600
Your breath probably stank 
while you were asleep.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:44.930
It's no good.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.800
I can't get the same color this way.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:52.260
It won't fool anybody!

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:56.360
You can only get that color 
off of a living human.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.650
Damn it! I can't do it!

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:00.570
I just can't do it!

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:02.130
Keep at it, Edogai-kun.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:03.060
Concentrate! Concentrate!

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:07.110
Okay, Tsukishima-san! Should I 
tattoo you and then rip off your skin?

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:11.280
Where's Tsurumi-san? I want to see him!

00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:13.750
Lt. Tsurumi returned to Otaru.

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:17.310
I'm only taking orders from him, got it?

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:20.850
Bring Tsurumi-san here!

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:22.790
Bring him here!

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:29.840
<b>Otaru</b>

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:32.420
<b>Takagi Arms Shop</b>

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:34.440
Your friend there doesn't look Ainu.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:36.140
Are those soldiers' clothes 
underneath that jacket?

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:40.100
Just give me bullets for this Murata gun.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:44.900
You know, an Ainu woman 
was here not long ago.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:49.000
She asked if I knew of a village where 
an Ainu girl with blue eyes lived.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.990
Didn't your niece have eyes like that?

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.990
What was she like?

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:57.480
She was pretty.

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.960
I think she said she was a fortune-teller.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:04.810
You're walking a lot better now.

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:05.950
Yeah.

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:07.870
It barely hurts at all now.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:10.690
What will you do now, Tanigaki?

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.410
Want to kill it before we go home?

00:17:17.410 --> 00:17:18.720
It'll make a nice present.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:22.930
That bird's ripping off its winter 
coat to take back to its nest.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:26.520
Good... the deer hasn't noticed us yet.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:34.490
Yes!

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:41.910
I was going to aim for the neck.

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:44.040
We got interrupted.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.250
Still, nice job getting it in a single shot.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.270
Is that a boy from the village?

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:49.420
I've never seen him before.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:51.160
He's a weirdo.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.950
He never plays with the 
rest of the village kids.

00:17:52.950 --> 00:17:55.380
But he's interested in the hunt.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:18:03.060
Tanigaki's kid, Genjirou, put on a straw 
coat and followed the hunt again!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:06.820
If you want to watch from up closer,

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:08.310
gather up some pine boughs.

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:16.240
The front legs of a yuk are only connected 
by muscle, so they're easy to detach.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.040
This is yours.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.700
Really?

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.830
I can see you were born an Ani Matagi.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.080
You know just how it's done.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:31.040
Why was this tiny yuk all alone?

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:33.490
It's a male, so it must've 
just left its parents.

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:35.460
Or maybe they died.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:38.220
Then it's just like me, huh?

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.850
His siblings and parents all died.

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.160
All the old people in the 
village take care of him.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.980
His real name is...

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:50.190
Your parents gave it to you 
before they died, right?

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:51.430
Cikapasi!

00:18:51.430 --> 00:18:52.740
Great name, huh?

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:53.720
Yeah.

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:56.030
Cikapasi? What does that mean?

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:58.570
"He who makes birds fly."

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:02.030
But it also means "to get an erection."

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:04.780
In other words, "boner"?

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:08.330
You really do have a good name, Cikapasi.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.980
It's a great name, "boner."

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:20.290
Ayapo!

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.260
Anpene!

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:23.010
Iyainuman.

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:28.890
Oh, look at this wonderful Nispa.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:32.850
I love men with scars on their faces.

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:36.000
My name is Inkarmat.

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:37.820
It means "the woman who sees."

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:40.440
You there, the handsome Nispa.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:41.840
Shall I tell your fortune?

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.570
No, I'll pass.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:48.950
Did you lose your little sister?

00:19:50.890 --> 00:19:54.760
The thought came to me as I looked at you.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.060
I'm very sorry.

00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.840
Who are you?

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:04.570
I came here in search of someone.

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:08.860
Is there a girl with blue 
eyes who lives in this kotan?

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:11.850
My Sirakki Kamuy says 
this is the right place.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.310
We met in Naganuma.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.740
She said she was traveling 
to accomplish a certain goal.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:20.780
She had three Nispa with her.

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:28.200
One of them is going to betray Asirpa-san.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.880
He's a very dangerous man.

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:38.380
If he's not stopped,
her life may be in danger.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.590
I'll bring back Asirpa safely. I promise.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:54.310
Osoma, you have something to give him, right?

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:02.170
She spent a long time trying to make 
you tekunpe, with Huci's help.

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:04.440
She only managed to get 
one done in time, though.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:10.020
When an Ainu woman's in love, she makes 
a pair of tekunpe and gives them to her man.

00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:11.590
Thank you, Osoma.

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:13.200
I promise I'll come back.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.960
So make me the other one.

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:23.170
Gods, protect Tanigaki Nispa!

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:28.250
Shall I tell your fortune to
 help find where Asirpa-san is?

00:21:28.250 --> 00:21:33.110
No. I'm not going because I 
believe your fortune-telling.

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:37.080
The problem is that the villagers do.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:41.770
The Sirakki Kamuy tells me that 
good fortune lies to the east.

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:44.180
Let us go, Tanigaki Nispa.

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:46.450
Why are you coming with me?

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:52.040
I have a weakness for men 
with scars on their faces.

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:55.580
I see.

00:21:56.100 --> 00:22:00.040
Use the man named Tanigaki 
who's at the kotan.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:03.930
His leg should have healed by now.

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Fake</b>

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:39.380
Next Time: "Fake."
